      "title": "AI Is Not the Same for Everyone: How to Measure AI Readiness | Kian Katanforoosh, Workera",
      "summary": "Most companies have deployed AI tools across their organizations, but very few actually know who on their team can use them effectively, or how ready their workforce is for what's coming. Kian Katanforoosh, CEO & founder of Workera and adjunct lecturer at Stanford, has built a skills intelligence platform designed to change that. Workera assesses AI readiness at scale, maps skill gaps by role, and guides employees toward personalized learning, not through courses, but through a system that tells you exactly where you stand and what to do next. In this episode, Craig and Kian go deep on how enterprises like Accenture and the U.S. Space Force are using Workera to surface hidden talent, benchmark their teams against industry peers, and build AI fluency across every level of the organization. They also discuss Ambient - Workera's new ambient coaching product that learns from how you actually work - and what the company's acquisition by Pearson means for the future of skills assessment from the enterprise all the way down to K\u201312. Subscribe to Eye on A.I. for weekly conversations with the people building and deploying the future of AI.",
